  "gaps": [
    "The judgment does not explicitly rule on the hypothetical legal effect of acquiescence if it were actually proved, noting it was not necessary to decide as acquiescence was not established.",
    "The dissenting opinion by Sarkar J. argued that the 1958 Act should apply retrospectively to pending proceedings, a view rejected by the majority but not definitively overruled as binding precedent for all future cases involving different statutory contexts."
